// File: orchestrator/v1/orchestrator.proto
// Package orchestrator.v1 is the release control plane: bundle ingestion and
// artifact events, release definitions, customers and clusters, operator and
// enrollment records, artifact routing, values revisions and their approval
// flow, release operations with a watched timeline, inventory observation, the
// guard rails around the emergency entry point, and the retention-facing
// queries that support all of that.
// release-orchestrator serves BundleService and OrchestratorService on its
// management listener (dev port 8083) for the browser console, CI and
// administrative tooling. The customer-cluster operator agent reaches only one
// procedure, SyncInventory, and only over the mTLS agent-gateway listener (dev
// port 8084); everything else on this service is management-plane traffic.
// Management-plane calls carry a bearer access token or the console's access
// cookie. The shared interceptor requires that any organization_id in the
// request match the token, maps each procedure to a Casbin object and action
// (release, bundle, customer, binding, operator), and refuses any procedure it
// cannot map, so a new RPC needs a policy mapping before it can be called.
// Writes to release state are further gated by the caller's capability set and
// by an explicit authorization snapshot, and most are rejected while the
// orchestrator runs in maintenance mode.
// Every mutation is either keyed by the Idempotency-Key request header or by a
// natural key in the message; version fields are compare-and-swap tokens. Read
// surfaces are paginated with an opaque cursor and a page size clamped to
// [1, 100].

